    ],
    "rows": 10
   }
  ],
  "footnotes": [
   "Note.—In case two or more diseases breakout simultaneously in one and the same person, the disease named earlier in the above table is treated as the principal one. For instance, if a person is affected with both syphilis and gonorrhea, she is counted under \"Syphilis,\" although again she is counted in parantheses under \"Gonorrhea.\" Again, if a person is simultaneously affected with gonorrhea, ulcus molle and trachom, she is counted under \"Gonorrhea,\" although she is again counted in parantheses under both \"Ulcus molle\" and \"Trachom.\" This is the case with other diseases."
  ]
